  << /ActualText (Healthy male or female subjects\054 between the age of 18 and 55 years\054 both inclusive \050healthy is defined as no clinically relevant abnormalities identified by a detailed medical history\054 full physical examination\054 including blood pressure and heart rate measurement\054 12\055lead ECG\054 and clinical laboratory tests prior to administration of the study drug\051\056 Subject is informed and able to understand the full nature and purpose of the study\054 including possible risks and side effects\054 and is given ample time and opportunity to read and understand this information\056 Subject has the ability and agrees to cooperate with the Investigator and must sign and date the written informed consent prior to performing any of the screening procedures\056 BMI between 18\0560 and 32\0560 kg\057m2\054 both inclusive\056 Subject and their partner of childbearing potential must agree to use a highly effective method of contraception throughout the study and for 5 months after the administration of assigned tre \056\056\056)
